# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: cli-options-host-default-is-deprecated-mock — the --host default is stored as the deprecated alias :mock
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-cli-options-host-default
#+DATE: 2026-11-13

* Context

Found while answering "what is the default of --host?" (see
=cli-option-environment-defaults=). The documented default is =cador=
(=clautolisp --help=: "cador (default)"; =*host-descriptions*=).

* Problem

The shared =cli-options= struct initialises the slot to the deprecated alias:

: (host :mock)   ; AC  :mock / :null (default :mock)
  — =clautolisp/autolisp-cli/source/options.lisp=

- clautolisp maps =:mock= to cador when it builds the host, so the run is
  right, but =*AUTOLISP-HOST*= is rendered from the keyword: with no
  =--host= it reads =MOCK=, a name no =--host= spelling produces
  (=--host mock= gives =CADOR=). Observed on the installed clautolisp 1.8.59;
  the 2.4.3 source has the same code.
- The aliases =null= / =none= yield =:null= where =nihil= yields =:nihil=:
  =*AUTOLISP-HOST*= reads =NULL= for one spelling of the host and =NIHIL= for
  the other.
- The slot comment is stale (=:mock= / =:null=).
- Correction (2026-11-14): the first version of this ticket said alfe shows
  =host: MOCK= under =--dry-run=. It does not: alfe builds its options with
  =(make-cli-options :host :cador)= and rejects the retired spellings, so
  =alfe --dry-run= prints =host: CADOR=. Only clautolisp is affected.

* Proposal

Default the slot to =:cador=, update its comment, and fold the =null= /
=none= aliases onto =:nihil=.

* Acceptance criteria

- A test asserts the default host keyword is =:cador= and renders as
  =CADOR=.
- =--host null=, =--host none= and =--host nihil= all render as =NIHIL=.
- RELEASE_NOTES entry (the dry-run output changes); version bump.

* Resolved (clautolisp / alfe 2.4.8, 2026-11-14)

- =cli-options= host slot defaults to =:cador=; =parse-host= folds =null= /
  =none= onto =:nihil= (=clautolisp/autolisp-cli/source/options.lisp=).
  clautolisp's host constructor still accepts =:mock= / =:null= (a caller
  may build options by hand), so nothing that ran changes: only the name
  =*AUTOLISP-HOST*= shows.
- Tests (=autolisp-cli/tests/cli-launch-tests.lisp=):
  =default-host-is-cador=, =host-aliases-name-the-host-they-stand-for=, and
  =parse-host-accepts-cador-cadtui-nihil-and-aliases= now expects =:nihil=
  for the aliases. All three failed before the fix.
- clautolisp user manual (=*AUTOLISP-HOST*= entry, which still said
  =MOCK-HOST= / =NULL-HOST=) and RELEASE_NOTES updated.
